Let me restate the translation accurately:

{127} That is: the hypocrites, who are wary lest a surah be sent down exposing what is in their hearts. When a surah is sent down so that they might believe in it and act upon its content, {they glance at one another}, resolved to abandon acting upon it, seeking an opportunity to slip away from the sight of the believers, and saying: {Does anyone see you?} Then {they turn away}, slipping off and turning aside in aversion. So God requited them with a punishment of the same kind as their deeds: just as they turned away from acting, {God turned their hearts away}; that is, He repelled them from the truth and forsook them, {because they are a people who do not understand}, with an understanding that would benefit them. For had they understood, when a surah was sent down they would have believed in it and submitted to its command. The purpose of this is to show the intensity of their aversion to jihad and to other laws of faith, as God Most High said about them: {And when a decisive surah is sent down and fighting is mentioned in it, you see those in whose hearts is a disease looking at you with the look of one fainting from death.}
